From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:23:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show text inputs' placeholders in the `::placeholder` style

An `<input>` or `<textarea>` with a `placeholder` showed nothing while
empty. Its placeholder now shows while the value is empty and no IME
composition is in progress (an empty value with a preedit shows the
preedit, not the placeholder), under the caret, in the `::placeholder`
style: Stylo computes that pseudo-element lazily, so it is resolved when
the input's editor is built, and its colour (with its opacity) paints
the text. A single-line input's placeholder loses its line breaks, as
HTML says, and is centred as the input's text is.

The UA sheet gives `::placeholder` Chromium's light grey (#757575).
Changing the `placeholder` attribute rebuilds the input's box, as
`value` does.
